Hello Saarang,

Your feedback from the interview process continues to be strong and we=E2=
=80=99re excited to move you forward to the next stage! =F0=9F=98=8A

For the next portion of the process, please find attached the case study da=
taset and FAQs. Below you will find the full instructions and guidance to s=
upport your preparation.

We kindly ask that you submit your completed presentation within 7 days. On=
ce submitted, the hiring team will review your materials and confirm whethe=
r you will be proceeding to the presentation round with the Supply Analytic=
s interview panel.

Please acknowledge receipt of this email.

Case Study Instructions

You should prepare a PowerPoint presentation designed for a senior executiv=
e audience.

The presentation should be structured, concise, and focused on both strong =
analytics and strategic recommendations.

Please ensure your presentation:

* Clearly outlines the data analysis you conducted
* Highlights key findings and insights
* Explicitly states any assumptions you have made
* Explains how you would validate these assumptions if implemented
* Includes a clear Executive Summary slide with recommendations

Most new features launched on the Agoda website aim to increase the number =
of bookings. One way to improve conversion is by encouraging customers to c=
omplete their bookings quickly through a call-to-action known internally as=
 an =E2=80=9Curgency message.=E2=80=9D

Examples:

* =E2=80=9CPrices have been rising. Book now to lock in your rates!=E2=80=
=9D
* =E2=80=9CYour check-in is fast approaching. Book now to lock in your rate=
s!=E2=80=9D

A Product Owner would like to explore implementing urgency messaging and ha=
s requested an analysis to understand how prices move as the booking date a=
pproaches the check-in date, and what business opportunities may arise from=
 these findings.

Attached is a randomly sampled dataset from five different cities with chec=
k-in dates between 01/10/2016 =E2=80=93 31/12/2016.

There is no limitation on tools or technology for this analysis.

Important Guidance for This Round

Please note that historically, the majority of candidates did not pass the =
case review stage. We strongly encourage you to put in extra effort for thi=
s assignment =F0=9F=98=8A.

Based on previous reviews, cases typically fell short due to:

* Weak or incomplete exploratory data analysis (EDA)
* Lack of depth and generality in the approach
* Limited or incorrect use of statistical methods
* Analysis not clearly connected to recommendations

To strengthen your submission, please ensure you include:

* =E2=9C=85 A clear Executive Summary

* =E2=9C=85 Thorough Exploratory Data Analysis (EDA) (this is a must-have)
* =E2=9C=85 A well-structured and professional deck
* =E2=9C=85 Clear, data-driven conclusions and recommendations
* =E2=9C=85 An assessment of business impact

Senior leadership will be looking not only at what you found, but also how =
rigorously you arrived at your conclusions and how clearly you translate an=
alysis into business decisions.

Points to Consider

You may reflect on (but are not limited to) the following:

* At which stage of the funnel should urgency messaging be implemented?
(Homepage, search results page, property page, or booking form?)
* What assumptions are you making?
* What factors influence price movement?
* What limitations exist in the dataset?
* What additional data would strengthen the analysis?
* What conclusions can you draw?
* What recommendations would you provide to the Product Owner?

Presentation Expectations

If shortlisted, you will have approximately 30 minutes to present your find=
ings and recommendations to management, followed by approximately 30 minute=
s of Q&A.

To support your preparation:

* Build a compelling narrative =E2=80=94 not just analysis slides
* Focus on the =E2=80=9Cso what?=E2=80=9D for each slide
* Provide clear, top-down, actionable recommendations
* Maintain clarity, confidence, and executive presence

Our management team is highly analytical and data-driven, so accuracy, logi=
cal reasoning, and structured thinking are essential.

Data Dictionary

# =E2=80=93 Number of records in each dataset
ADR =E2=80=93 Average Daily Rate in USD (Customer Total Amount / Room Night=
s)
Hotel ID =E2=80=93 Property identification number
City ID =E2=80=93 City identification number
Star Rating =E2=80=93 Property star rating
Accommodation Type Name =E2=80=93 Property=E2=80=99s accommodation type
Chain Hotel =E2=80=93 Indicates whether the property is part of a chain
Booking Date =E2=80=93 Date the booking was made
Check-in Date =E2=80=93 Date of check-in
Check-out Date =E2=80=93 Date of check-out

Please let us know if you have any questions, and best of luck with your pr=
eparation!

